# panda-social-cc-agent (standalone deploy repo) NOTE — differs from upstream:
#
# In the panda monorepo this directory is GITIGNORED and regenerated at build
# time by scripts/build/build-skill-runtimes.sh, which rsyncs the canonical
# packages/cadpy/src/cadpy/ tree here. THIS repo has no canonical cadpy in its
# build context, so the cadquery cadpy is VENDORED AND COMMITTED here instead.
#
# Why it must exist: the cadcode runner inserts scripts/packages on sys.path and
# does `import cadpy` (see ../../common/runner.py). With this dir empty the import
# falls through to the build123d-based cad-viewer cadpy that the Dockerfile
# pip-installs globally — which rejects cadquery shapes, so EVERY remix fails.
# This cadquery cadpy (module-level generate_step, accepts cq.Workplane) is what
# the runner was written for.
#
# Re-vendor on cadpy updates (from a checkout of the panda monorepo):
#   rsync -a --delete --exclude=__pycache__ --exclude='*.pyc' \
#     --filter='P README.md' --filter='P .gitignore' \
#     <panda>/packages/cadpy/src/cadpy/  skills/cadcode/scripts/packages/cadpy/
#
# Vendored from panda/packages/cadpy @ commit 0eb65fd (matches the skill files
# synced from that same panda commit for web-create desktop parity).
# KEEP IN SYNC WITH THE SKILL: re-vendor from the panda commit whose cadcode skill
# files (runner.py, cadlib/, SKILL.md, examples) this repo matches — NOT blindly from
# HEAD. A cadpy from a different commit than the skill is a latent mismatch (we shipped
# an older #13 cadpy under a #40 skill once; it worked, but only by luck of a stable API).
# Keep only caches out of git:
__pycache__/
*.pyc
